//@version=6
// Market Structure 1-2-3  |  v1  (structure only, no entry models)
// v4.48: FIX missing trend shift after an MSS. v4.43 required an established BOS (the 3) before the anti-directional count could start. After an MSS the
//        new trend often has NO BOS yet: price retests the three levels (SBR / QML / L3) and builds a minor anti-directional structure there
//        (A-B-C-D, fifth leg = body close beyond C). With the BOS rule that structure was never counted, so the shift back (e.g. to bullish) was
//        not marked and the status box stayed on "waiting for a retracement". The count now also starts from a confirmed retracement while the
//        trend is still in its post-MSS state (levels being tested). A plain retest of a level is still NOT called anti-directional: A, B, C
//        and the shift appear only when a real minor structure forms (confirmed retracement -> A -> body close beyond A -> retracement -> C ->
//        body close beyond C). The status box now says "levels being tested" for that stage instead of an anti-directional wording.
// v4.47: Level 2 "Zone Marking Off / On" checked end to end. Both modes use the same zone candle (red candle with the lowest close between the
//        high and the BOS); the only difference is the bottom edge: OFF = lowest low from that candle up to and including the BOS candle,
//        ON = the candle's own low. A doji is marked whole in ON, and in OFF unless its wick reaches Level 1 (open down to the low). FIX: the
//        anti-directional B zone found through the swing-pivot path ignored this setting (always OFF-style); it now follows it, like the B zone of
//        the main anti-directional path. Setting title / tooltip reworded so the two states are unmistakable.
// v4.46: ALL zones (Level 1 / Level 2, SBR / QML / L3, Double / Triple MSS) follow one length rule: a zone starts at its own candle, grows candle by
//        candle and is closed by the existing rules (first retracement / BOS of the new trend, or a close through the zone). No zone is drawn
//        into the empty space to the right of the last candle any more. NEW settings (group "Zones"): shift the START edge and the END edge of
//        every zone forward (+) or backward (-) in candles (set both to the same value to move whole zones), and an optional maximum length.
// v4.45: Double / Triple MSS zones no longer extend into the empty space to the right of the last candle. They are drawn only up to the
//        latest candle (growing with each new candle) until the new trend's first retracement / BOS closes them (v4.44 rule). Before, while
//        no retracement had formed yet, they were extended to infinity on the right.
// v4.44: Double / Triple MSS zones (e.g. "MSS2 double top", "MSS2 SBR", "MSS4 upper") no longer run on to the right edge. They now end at the same
//        moment as the SBR / QML / L3 zones: at the first retracement (or the first BOS) of the new trend. The third-MSS / flip logic still
//        watches the far edge of the far zone, only the drawn boxes are shortened. Nothing else changed.
// v4.43: FIX A / B / C appearing without a real retracement (anti-directional count started too early).
//        Order now enforced: (1) the trend has an established BOS (the 3); (2) a retracement of the trend is CONFIRMED after it; (3) that
//        counter-move becomes the anti-directional impulse and the anti-directional engine starts only AFTER the confirming candle (before, it
//        started at the retracement's first candle, so candles inside the confirmation window could already count as "the retracement of the
//        impulse" and place A); (4) A = top of that impulse, placed when a retracement of the impulse is confirmed; (5) B = Level 2 zone after
//        the first body close beyond A; (6) C = top placed by the next confirmed retracement; (7) a body close beyond C shifts the trend.
//        The status box now shows the real A / B-zone / C prices once a shift has happened, so a wrong mark can be checked at once.
// v4.42: FIX position of B. B is no longer drawn on the candle that first closes beyond A: it is the LEVEL 2 ZONE created by that break
//        (same rule as the main Level 2 zone, mirrored for the anti-directional move: the countertrend candle with the lowest close between A
//        and the breaking candle, from its OPEN to the lowest low up to the break). B is labelled on that zone and the zone is drawn.
// v4.41: FIX anti-directional A-B-C (a trend shift was triggered although no real retracement had formed).
//        (1) Counting starts only from a CONFIRMED retracement of the trend (after the 3): an unconfirmed single candle / pending inside bar no
//            longer starts it (input below can restore the old behaviour).
//        (2) Minor structure: swing pivots are accepted only from the retracement's first candle on (before: from the trend's extreme, so a tiny
//            bounce right after the 3 became "A").
//        (3) A is valid only once a retracement has formed after it (a candle body closes below the previous candle's low after the A high).
//            B = first body close beyond A. C is valid only once a retracement has formed after it. The trend shifts only on a body close beyond C.
// v4.40: LEVEL 2 zone + MSS line to the written rule. Candle = the red candle with the LOWEST CLOSE between point 1 (the swing high) and the
//        BOS candle. Zone = from that candle's OPEN (was its close) down to the LOWEST LOW from that candle up to and including the BOS
//        candle. The MSS line now sits at that same lowest low (and the "2" / "MSS line" tag on its candle). Doji rule unchanged.
// v4.39: FIX Double MSS top zone height: bottom = the candle's CLOSE (a doji: its low, the whole candle), top = the HIGHEST POINT reached
//        before the retracement (the highest high from that candle up to the MSS), not only the candle's own high. Nothing else changed.
// v4.38: FIX Double MSS top zone (Double Top / Bottom): narrowed to the candle's CLOSE up to its HIGH (was open to high). Same candle
//        (highest close); a doji still marks the whole candle. Nothing else changed.
// v4.37: Double MSS zones changed to the written rules. After the two closes beyond the old extreme the TWO levels are:
//        (1) the Double Top / Double Bottom itself, as a SMALL zone: the candle with the highest close, open to its own high (a doji: the
//            whole candle) - no longer stretched to the highest high; (2) the SBR / RBS zone at the bottom: the lowest-close candle, from its
//            OPEN down to the lowest low. The three old levels (SBR, QML, L3) are faded out so the two new zones stand out.
//            The "upper zone from the shift candle's close" idea of v4.36 (and its "confirming / first close" input) is gone.
//            Third MSS and later flips unchanged from v4.36.
// v4.36: DOUBLE / TRIPLE MSS (new module, nothing else changed).
//        Double MSS = after an MSS, two closes beyond the old structure's extreme (double top / bottom) turn the trend back. The three
//        levels (SBR / QML / L3) are replaced by TWO refined zones for the returning trend (bullish example, bearish = mirror):
//          upper zone: from the CLOSE of the candle that triggered the shift up to the highest point reached before the retracement
//                      (it keeps growing until the first retracement of the new trend is confirmed);
//          lower zone: the red candle with the LOWEST CLOSE before the retracement: from its OPEN down to the lowest low reached.
//        The zones live until a new BOS forms (structure continues) or until mssN closes beyond the far edge of the far zone (lower
//        zone's bottom in a bullish trend) = THIRD MSS (trend flips again). Third MSS zones (bearish example):
//          top zone: the green candle with the highest close before the retracement: from its OPEN up to its HIGH (the old
//                    close-based top zone is dropped);
//          bottom zone: the previous lower zone, refined: same red candle, from its CLOSE (not open) down to the lowest low.
//        Further flips repeat the same rules (mirrored). Captions: MSS2 upper / lower, MSS3 upper / lower ...
// v4.35: a Level 1 zone with a Fair Value Gap (SBT3) is labelled SBT3 only - SBT-2 is no longer added next to it ("L1 / SBT3", or
//        "L1 / SBT5+SBT3" when a countertrend candle + gap also match). SBT-2 shows only when the zone has no gap. Nothing else changed.
// v4.34: SBT3 = any Fair Value Gap that overlaps the Level 1 zone (even partly), independent of SBT-2 / SBT5. The gap that makes an SBT5
//        is no longer excluded from SBT3, so a zone with a red candle + gap now reads "L1 / SBT5+SBT3" (bearish mirror: green candle + gap).
//        Nothing else changed.
// v4.32: SBT-2 scan widened: every countertrend candle from the structure's start up to the candle BEFORE the BOS candle is checked
//        (v4.31 stopped at the retracement's first candle, so a countertrend candle sitting in the Level 1 zone later in the leg that
//        breaks the structure was never seen - e.g. the green candle inside the latest bearish L1 box). Same overlap rules as before
//        (body overlap, doji by wick, touch tolerance). Nothing else changed.
// v4.31: (1) The orange "SBT3 FVG" tag is gone (the zone caption "L1 / SBT3" already says it) - both places it was drawn.
//        (2) SBT-2 now also looks at the retracement's FIRST candle when it is a spike (its extreme is the Level 1 level): a green
//        engulfing/spike candle in a bearish leg (red in a bullish leg) whose wick/body sits in the zone was never checked, because the
//        scan stopped one candle short. (3) New input: body-touch tolerance (% of the Level 1 zone height) for SBT-2 / SBT5, so a body
//        that opens a tick short of the zone edge still counts as touching. Caption then reads e.g. "L1 / SBT-2+SBT3".
// v4.30: (1) FIX SBT-1: the candle right after the Level 2 zone candle, when it is a bullish candle moving away from the zone, no longer
//        counts as "mitigation" (it opens at the zone's top, so its low always touched it and every such zone was labelled plain "L2").
//        (2) SBT5 gap rule widened to "a gap alongside the countertrend candle": the candle is candle 1 of the gap, OR candle 3 of the gap,
//        OR the candle immediately AFTER the gap. Body rule unchanged (input).
// v4.29: NEW SBT5 (Level 1 zone, bullish and bearish mirrored). A countertrend candle (red in a bullish leg / green in a bearish leg)
//        whose BODY sits inside the Level 1 zone AND is candle 1 of a 3-candle Fair Value Gap (next candle with the trend, candle 3 up to
//        and including the BOS candle, opens a gap beyond candle 1's extreme). Zone is labelled "L1 / SBT5". The same candle with NO gap
//        stays SBT-2. The gap SBT5 uses is not counted again as SBT3 (another, different gap on the zone still adds "+SBT3").
//        No extra candle tag is drawn for SBT5 (no duplicate text). New input: "SBT5: body must sit fully inside the Level 1 zone".
// v4.28: SBT 4 - removed the extra teal "SBT 4" tag on the candle (duplicate) and the trailing D/S on the zone caption; zone now reads just "L2 / SBT 4".
// v4.27: FIX runtime error RE10045 (Pine for-loops count DOWN when start > end: guarded). Zone caption is "L1 / SBT3" (no D/S, no second FVG word); the "SBT3 FVG" tag stays on the BOS candle.
//        Also: (1) SBT3 tag now sits on the BOS (market-structure-break) candle, text "SBT3 FVG". (2) "L2 / COND" removed: a
//        mitigated Level 2 zone is now just "L2". (3) NEW SBT 4: Level 2 zone with a Fair Value Gap right after it -
//        bullish middle candle (real green in a bullish leg / real red in a bearish leg), candle 1 = the last candle
//        that still touches Zone 2, candle 3 up to and including the BOS candle. Zone is labelled "L2 / SBT 4 D|S" and
//        a "SBT 4" tag is placed on that candle 1. No gap = unchanged "L2 / SBT-1 D|S".
// v4.26: SBT-3 fix #2 - a Fair Value Gap whose MIDDLE candle is the BOS (breakout) candle itself was never found: its
//        3rd candle is the candle AFTER the BOS, which does not exist yet when the zone is drawn. The zone is now
//        re-checked one candle later; if that gap overlaps Level 1 the label is upgraded to "L1 / ... SBT-3 FVG D/S"
//        and the orange "FVG" tag is placed on the BOS candle. Nothing else changed.
// v4.25: SBT-3 fix - the FVG's 3rd candle can now be the BOS candle itself (previously the scan stopped one candle
//        short of the BOS, so a gap whose 3rd candle was the actual breakout candle was never found). Everything
//        else about SBT-3 is unchanged.
// v4.24: SBT-1 and SBT-2 labelling added. Neither zone's position, size, or existing rules changed - this only names
//        them on the chart and adds one new check (mitigation) for SBT-1.
//        - Level 2 zone = SBT-1: "L2 / SBT-1 D" (Demand) in a bullish trend, "L2 / SBT-1 S" (Supply) in a bearish trend.
//          NEW: if any candle traded back into the zone AFTER it formed but BEFORE the BOS confirmed it, the zone is
//          "mitigated" and is labelled "L2 / COND" instead - SBT-1 does not apply to a mitigated zone.
//        - Level 1 zone = SBT-2, but ONLY when a countertrend candle (red, in a bullish leg / green, in a bearish
//          leg) sits inside the impulse leg BEFORE the BOS and overlaps the Level 1 zone: an ordinary candle must
//          overlap by its BODY, but a doji-type candle (wick longer than its body) qualifies on its WICK alone
//          (its full high-to-low range) reaching into the zone, even with no body overlap at all.
//        - Level 1 zone = SBT-3 when a 3-candle Fair Value Gap sits ANYWHERE before the BOS candle - this can
//          straddle the swing pivot or sit inside the retracement leg, not just the narrow impulse leg (unlike
//          SBT-2, which per the user's own wording stays impulse-only) - with a bullish middle candle (real green
//          in a bullish leg, real red in a bearish leg) AND the gap (candle 1's high .. candle 3's low) overlapping
//          the Level 1 zone at all, even partially.
//        - SBT-2 and SBT-3 are independent checks on the SAME Level 1 zone and can both be true at once. The label
//          lists whichever matched: "L1 / SBT-2 D", "L1 / SBT-3 FVG D", "L1 / SBT-2+SBT-3 FVG D" (bearish: " S"
//          instead of " D"). If neither matched, the zone is still drawn (it's still a valid Level 1 zone) but
//          stays labelled plain "L1" - it is not a valid SBT-2 or SBT-3 setup.
//        - NEW: whenever SBT-3 fires, a small orange "FVG" tag is placed on the exact middle candle the engine
//          used, with a tooltip giving the gap's real price range - so the match can be checked directly on the
//          chart (hover it) instead of guessed from a screenshot.
//        - Both zones keep working exactly as before otherwise: a successful retest (no close back out) means the
//          next candle's open is the entry (buy in a bullish trend, sell in a bearish trend); a close back out
//          invalidates the zone (grey, dotted) as before.
//        - NOT changed: when a trend shift (MSS) happens, the OLD Level 1 / Level 2 zones still get relabelled
//          "QML" / "SBR" / "RBS" for the new trend's reference levels, same as before v4.24 - their SBT-1 / SBT-2 /
//          COND labels are overwritten at that point. See the reply this version shipped with for why.
// Retracement setups: two-candle, engulfing, inside bar  ->  point 2
// Close beyond the level                                   ->  BOS (point 3)
// At each BOS: Level 1 / Level 2 zones, MSS line
// MSS (two closes beyond the MSS line)                     ->  trend shift + three levels (SBR/KML or RBS/QML, Level 3)
// Anti-directional 1-2-3-4-5 (five-wave) shift, fake-out / invalidation
// v4.23: nothing of the anti-directional A-B-C is drawn on the chart before the trend shifts (the status box carries it: A, B, C, D and the
//        price whose body close shifts the trend). When a candle body closes beyond C the legs A, B, C, D are marked on the chart (E, the fifth
//        leg, is the break itself); one bar later C is re-labelled 1 and the C-D segment 2, and the normal count continues with 3 ...
// v4.22: the trend shifts only on a candle BODY close beyond the C level = the extreme (low / high) of C, not the body of the C candle.
//        Before that nothing is shifted and no 1 / BOS / 2 is drawn for the anti-directional legs: they are marked A-B (together, when B
//        forms with the close beyond A) and C (when C forms). At the shift the old A-B is not re-marked as 1 / BOS / 2.
// v4.21: anti-directional tracking starts when a retracement BEGINS (also while it is still a valid inside bar), not only once it is
//        confirmed. This covers the bullish / bearish dealing range after a BOS, an inside bar inside a retracement, and the retests of the
//        three levels (SBR / RBS, QML, Level 3) after an MSS: five anti-directional waves (or five minor swings) shift the trend there too.
// v4.20: the status box now walks through A / B / C / Trend shift (A placed at a price, B formed when a body closes beyond A, C placed,
//        the trend shifts on a body close beyond C); nothing has to be drawn on the chart. After a five-wave shift the latest point is
//        marked "C", which becomes "1" when it is broken, followed by the "2" at the MSS-line low, and the count continues.
//        New colours: MSS label text, "MSS line" tag text, "2" label; new size: "2" label.
// v4.19: anti-directional marks follow a strict order: A when the retracement against the trend is confirmed (with its level line),
//        B only when a candle closes beyond A, C only after B exists. B is labelled "B" on the breaking candle.
// v4.18: Settings -> Text sizes: a size for each label type (1, 3, BOS, MSS, MSS line tag, 5th wave, zone captions, A/B/C)
//        or one switch to give all of them the same size.
// v4.17: "One colour for all zones" switch (L1, L2, Double Top, Double Bottom, SBR, QML, RBS) + one shared fill transparency;
//        SBR / RBS / QML / L3 are now drawn with identical fill, border and text settings.
// v4.16: colour boxes in Settings: (1) Zone Marking Level 1 / Level 2, (2) Double Top / Double Bottom / SBR / QML / RBS,
//        (3) "1" / BOS / MSS label / MSS line / "3", (4) text colours. The MSS line is always dotted.
// v4.15: new Settings -> Colours: Level 1 / Level 2 colour, the three-level colour (SBR/RBS, QML, L3), the "1" / BOS / MSS line colour
//        (the MSS line always uses the colour of the "1"), label text colour and zone text colour.
// v4.14: BOS label is smaller (tiny). Level 1 / Level 2 use one light sky-blue, the three levels after a shift (SBR / RBS, QML, Level 3)
//        use one light lavender - same colours in bullish and bearish. BOS and MSS lines + labels + the 5th-wave label share one colour,
//        lines are thinner (width 1) and these labels are tiny.
// v4.13: BS is now called BOS and has the colour of the "1" label (so does the BOS line); the MSS label is black; the MSS line keeps the
//        colour of the "1". SBR / RBS / QML are drawn as bold as Level 3 (same violet, stronger fill, solid thick border).
//        Minor structure: the counter-directional A-B-C is now also read from the minor swings (pivots) inside the retracement, so a
//        five-leg A-B-C-D-E zigzag against the trend (leg 5 = body close beyond the top of leg 3, after the pullback in leg 4) shifts the
//        trend like the candle-pattern count does. Same invalidation: two closes (or one large candle) beyond the low of leg 2.
// v4.12: BS / BOS colour is black. No "C broken" label: when the anti-directional C is broken the trend shifts, the shift is marked
//        once ("5th wave: trend shift") and the new structure is followed with the normal count (1, 2, 3 ...). Every label uses one
//        font size; the "MSS line" tag is plain outlined text; zones that were taken out are muted. Never A-B-C-D-A.
// v4.11: Level 2 zone rewritten to the written rules. Candle = red candle with the LOWEST CLOSE between the start of the retracement and
//        the BOS candle. "Zone Marking Off" (default): top = that close; bottom = the lowest low from that candle up to and including
//        the BOS (never further back - that is the MSS line). Doji-type candle (wicks longer than body, and its close is the lowest):
//        the whole candle, high to low - but if its wick reaches into Level 1, from its open down to the low. Large / engulfing candles
//        use the close like any other. "Zone Marking On": open down to the candle's own low (doji: the whole candle).
//        Level 1 and Level 2 share one colour; the three levels after a shift (SBR/RBS, QML, Level 3) share another.
// v4.10: Level 2 zone follows the four reference sketches. Candle = the red candle with the lowest close (retracement start .. BOS).
//        Engulfing (a red candle right after a green one that closes below that green candle's low, or covers its body), or a
//        large candle  -> zone from its CLOSE down to its LOW.   Doji-type (wicks longer than the body) -> the whole candle.
//        Any other candle -> from its OPEN down to the lowest low. Starts at that candle, runs to the right. Bearish = exact mirror.
// v4.9: the anti-directional A-B-C is only looked for once a proper retracement of the trend has been confirmed (point 1-2 of the
//       main engine, phase 1). A small bounce that has not retraced is not an A. The anti-directional engine starts at the first
//       candle of that retracement. Level 2 zone: if the lowest-close candle is an engulfing candle, the zone runs from its close to its low.
// v4.8: the MSS line and its "MSS line" tag use the same dark slate as the 1 / 2 / 3 labels (the MSS event label stays violet).
// v4.7: anti-directional wording is A-B-C: A = the retracement against the trend (level), B = a candle BODY closes beyond A (BS),
//       C = the pullback after B; a body close beyond C shifts the trend. Nothing is drawn for it until the shift (unless the setting
//       is on); the status box carries the note. The "2" at the MSS line is now a small "MSS line" tag. "3-1" is written as just "1".
// v4.6: anti-directional waves are NOT drawn on the chart until the fifth wave completes the shift (setting "Anti-Directional 1-2-3"
//       is OFF by default; ON = draw A1-A4 as they form). The status box reports progress in words: forming / one sequence formed
//       (a candle body closed beyond the A level) / second forming with the price that completes the fifth wave / A5 placed.
// v4.5: FIX "Latest": after a trend shift (MSS or five waves) the view now keeps the structure that was shifted (its L1 / L2 zones,
//       SBR / RBS, QML, Level 3, MSS) together with the new trend, instead of cutting everything at the shift candle.
//       New setting "Mark directional 1-2-3" (OFF by default): the 1 / 2 / 3 / BS marks of the trend's own direction are no longer drawn;
//       only the anti-directional A1-A5 marks are. Zones, MSS and the levels stay. When the fifth wave completes, the new structure is drawn.
// v4.4: FIX the vertical line: a level line whose two points fall on the same candle (point 1 or the MSS-line low on the current bar)
//       was drawn as a vertical line running down the chart. The second point is now always at least one tick later.
//       Anti-directional waves are labelled A1 A2 (with A-BS), A3 A4 and A5, are ON by default, and the table walks through
//       A1-A2 -> break -> A3-A4 -> A5 (with the price that completes the fifth wave).
// v4.3: Level 2 zone covers the whole candle (high to low) when that candle is a doji type (wick longer than the body).
//       New setting "Anti-Directional 1-2-3": when ON, the anti-directional 1-2-3 is marked as soon as its first break (one entry) appears
//       and its 3 when the pullback forms; when OFF (default) nothing anti-directional is marked until the fifth wave completes the shift.
//       Status table trimmed to Trend / MSS line (with the exact price and direction) / Anti-directional (progress) / Marking.
// v4.2: MSS line and BS line are thicker so they stand out. The BS label sits in the centre of its Level 1 zone.
//       The status table now shows the real wave progress of the new trend (1/5 ... 5/5) and what price has to do next, with the price.
// v4.1: zone captions (L1, L2, QML, SBR / RBS, L3 ...) sit in the exact centre of their zone. Level 2 zones (the loose / unrefined area
//       around the MSS line) and zones that were taken out are drawn with a dotted border; Level 1 / QML and Level 3 stay solid.
// v4.0: new "Marking" setting. "Full Marking" draws the whole structure over the chart (as before). "Latest" keeps only the current
//       structure (the most recent 1-2 / 1-2-BS, its zones, MSS line, pending 3 and any active SBR/QML/L3 levels) and removes everything older.
//       Works on any timeframe. The status table shows the active mode.
// v3.9: Level 3 (double top / bottom after an MSS): if the chosen candle is a doji-type candle (wicks longer than the body) the zone
//       covers the WHOLE candle, low to high; otherwise open to high as before. Zone captions and labels are bigger and theme-safe.
// v3.8: every label sits on the candle where its event happened. MSS (and "trend back") is marked on the FIRST close beyond the
//       MSS line, and the MSS line ends on that candle. Cleaner palette, lighter zones, short zone captions.
// v3.7: point 2 is only marked once the BOS has happened. While the retracement is pending (no BOS yet) only the high is
//       labelled "3" (or "1" for the very first structure); at the BOS it becomes "3-1" and the "2" is placed at the MSS-line low.
// v3.6: FIX - every BOS is now marked (1, 2, BS, MSS line, L1/L2 zones), also right after an MSS / trend back / five-wave shift.
//       Cause 1: the v3.3 rule hid all structure of the new trend until five waves were complete (now an option, off by default).
//       Cause 2: when the engine was rebuilt after a shift, BOS events inside the replayed bars were swallowed and never drawn.
// v3.5: trend back needs two closes beyond the old structure's extreme (double top / bottom). Level 1 after a shift is labelled QML.
// v3.3: after a trend shift by MSS, the new trend's 1-2 (entry) is NOT marked until five waves are complete.
//       The BS label sits inside the Level 1 zone.
// v3: the level (BS line, Level 1 zone top) is the highest high INCLUDING the first retracement candle (spike that closes red).
//     Two ways to shift the trend: five anti-directional waves, or two closes beyond the MSS line (switch in the settings).
// v2: main structure only. Points 1 and 2 are marked when the retracement is confirmed; the BS line sits at the level of
//     the high (3-1) from that moment until a candle BODY closes beyond it. A deeper retracement no longer discards the main structure.
// Bearish logic is the exact mirror of bullish (candles are mirrored internally).
indicator("Market Structure 1-2-3 (v4.48)", shorttitle = "MS 1-2-3", overlay = true, max_boxes_count = 500, max_lines_count = 500, max_labels_count = 500)

// ───────────────────────────── Inputs
mssN     = input.int(2, "Closes beyond the MSS line", minval = 1, group = "Rules")
ratio    = input.float(2.0, "Large candle ratio (Level 2 zone and invalidation)", minval = 1.0, step = 0.5, group = "Rules")
useRange = input.bool(false, "Measure candle size by range (off = body)", group = "Rules")
mssFlip  = input.bool(true, "Trend shift 2: two closes beyond the MSS line (the other shift is five anti-directional waves)", group = "Rules")
